cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use synthcheck, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "synthcheck: Tests How Authentic Synthetic Survey Respondents Look"
abstract: >-
  An R package that tests whether synthetic respondents generated by large
  language models resemble the real survey respondents they are meant to
  stand in for. Overlap shows whether synthetic respondents land where real
  people land, Structure whether the items relate to each other as they do in
  real people, and Behaviour whether synthetic respondents answer the way
  people do. Each index is anchored between a shuffled baseline and a second
  sample of real people, and the synthetic authenticity benchmark compares
  several models in one table. The package compares models and supports
  decisions about them, and it does not show that synthetic data can replace
  a field test.
